      "text": "The sequence given is an arithmetic series with the first term $a_1=1$, common difference $d=6$, and the last term $a_n=259$. To find the number of terms $n$ in the series, we use the formula for the $n$th term of an arithmetic series:\n\n\\[a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d\\]\n\nPlugging in the values, we have:\n\n\\[259 = 1 + (n-1) \\times 6\\]\n\nSolving for $n$:\n\n\\[259 = 1 + 6n - 6\\]\n\\[259 = 6n - 5\\]\n\\[6n = 264\\]\n\\[n = 44\\]\n\nNow, to find the remainder when the sum $S_n$ of the arithmetic series is divided by $6$, we start with the formula for the sum of the first $n$ terms of an arithmetic series:\n\n\\[S_n = \\frac{n}{2} (a_1 + a_n)\\]\n\nPlugging in the values $n=44$, $a_1=1$, and $a_n=259$, we get:\n\n\\[S_{44} = \\frac{44}{2} (1 + 259)\\]\n\\[S_{44} = 22 \\times 260\\]\n\nFinally, the remainder when $S_{44}$ is divided by $6$ is found by simplifying $\\frac{S_{44}}{6}$:\n\n\\[\\frac{S_{44}}{6} = \\frac{22 \\times 260}{6} = 22 \\times 43.33\\]\n\nSince $43.33$ is not an integer, we simplify $S_{44}$ by multiplying by $6 again to remove the remainder and consider only the divisibility:\n\n\\[S_{44} = 22 \\times 260 = 5720\\]\n\nNow, we find the remainder when $5720$ is divided by $6$:\n\n\\[5720 \\div 6 = 953 \\text{ with a remainder of } 2.\\]\n\nTherefore, the remainder when the sum $1 + 7 + 13 + 19 + \\cdots + 253 + 259$ is divided by $6$ is $\\boxed{2}$.",
